Subject: [PATCH] zink: keep the visible-VRAM heap host-visible when there is none

When the device has no memory type that is both device-local and
host-visible, the screen filled ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_VISIBLE with the
DEVICE_LOCAL types. Zink uses that heap for buffers it maps directly:
PIPE_USAGE_DEFAULT and DYNAMIC buffers, and persistent and coherent
buffers (update_alloc_info_flags). Their memory was then not
host-visible, and zink_buffer_map still mapped them directly for
unsynchronized and plain write maps. On Venus, vkMapMemory of such memory
asks the host for a mappable blob of non-exportable memory ("vkr: mem is
not exportable"), the map fails, and the application crashes (Unigine
Heaven and Valley with OpenGL: an access violation in viogpu_wgl.dll).

A Venus guest on an RTX 5090 without resizable BAR has no such type once
patch 0070 (nvva) hides the host's small BAR heap. Fill the heap with the
HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT types instead, so that everything Zink places there
stays mappable, in host memory. Images whose memoryTypeBits exclude those
types are already demoted to DEVICE_LOCAL in allocate_bo(). Devices with a
device-local, host-visible type are unaffected.

Evidence: docs/unigl.md, docs/evidence/unigl/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d unigl worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
index 9084c91..87739f6 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3521,6 +3521,16 @@ zink_internal_create_screen(const struct pipe_screen_config *config, int64_t dev
          if (i == ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT_CACHED) {
             memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT]);
             screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT];
+         } else if (i == ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_VISIBLE) {
+            /* No CPU-visible VRAM. Buffers in this heap are mapped directly
+             * (persistent and coherent maps, unsynchronized and plain write
+             * maps), so the heap must stay host-visible: use host memory.
+             * Images that cannot live there are demoted to DEVICE_LOCAL by
+             * their memoryTypeBits.
+             */
+            memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT]);
+            screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT];
+            maybe_has_rebar = false;
          } else {
             memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL]);
             screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL];
